---
// Type: the web scale of base.css, the document scale of doc.css, the fonts and the prompt.
import DarkR from "../DarkR.astro";
import Notes from "./Notes.astro";

const tiers = `
:root {
  --r-font-heading: Audiowide, Rajdhani, sans-serif; /* h1, and h2 to h3 by default */
  --r-font-sub: var(--r-font-heading);               /* h2 to h3 */
  --r-font-minor: var(--r-font-text);                /* h4 to h6 */
}
/* Rajdhani for h2 and h3 only: */
:root { --r-font-sub: var(--r-font-text); }`;

const doc = `
<link rel="stylesheet" href="theme/doc.css">

<article class="r-doc">
  <h1>Mission control</h1>
  <p>Long text reads in Saira, at most 68 characters wide.</p>
</article>`;

const fonts = `
fonts/woff2/Enterprsr-Regular.woff2    Enterprsr, the ® of the name and the footer word
fonts/woff2/Audiowide-Regular.woff2    Audiowide, headings
fonts/woff2/Rajdhani-Medium.woff2      Rajdhani 500, text
fonts/woff2/Rajdhani-SemiBold.woff2    Rajdhani 600, labels and buttons
fonts/woff2/MonaspaceNeon.woff2        Monaspace Neon, code
fonts/woff2/Saira.woff2                Saira roman, document body (doc.css)
fonts/woff2/Saira-Italic.woff2         Saira italic, document body (doc.css)`;

const prompt = `<span class="r-prompt">Click or press</span>`;
---
<section class="sc-section" id="type">
  <h2 class="sc-label">Type</h2>
  <div class="sc-type">
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h1</b> Audiowide, Green</span><h1>Mission control</h1>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h2</b> Audiowide, Bright</span><h2>A quiet view from orbit</h2>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h3</b> Audiowide, Magenta</span><h3>Engineering log</h3>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h4</b> label caps, Amber</span><h4>Surfaces</h4>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h5</b> label caps, Light</span><h5>Instruments</h5>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>h6</b> label caps, Dark</span><h6>Footnotes</h6>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Body</b> Rajdhani 1.2rem</span><p>We build small, careful things and send them a long way. This is how body text reads on our dark background.</p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Small</b></span><small>info<span class="at">@</span>enterprise-r.com · small print and captions</small>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Link</b></span><p>Read the <a href="#type">mission notes</a> before you start.</p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Mark</b></span><p>The <mark>launch window</mark> opens at dawn.</p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Keys</b></span><p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>K</kbd> to search.</p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Prompt</b></span><p><span class="r-prompt">Click or press</span></p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Code</b></span><p><code>--r-text</code></p>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Quote</b></span><blockquote>Make it so, but make it small.</blockquote>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>List</b></span><ul><li>Plain lists keep the body text.</li><li>Nested items indent.</li></ul>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Definitions</b></span><dl><dt>Orbit</dt><dd>The path around a body.</dd><dt>Root</dt><dd>The lone R<span aria-hidden="true">, <span class="r-name-r">®</span></span>.</dd></dl>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Details</b></span><details><summary>Show the checklist</summary>Fuel, comms, crew.</details>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Figure</b></span><figure><img src="/assets/logo-wide.svg" width="320" height="56" alt="Enterprise-R"><figcaption>A figure scales down to its container.</figcaption></figure>
    <span class="sc-cap"><b>Selection</b></span><p>Select this line to see the selection colors.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="sc-note">Headings use Audiowide down to h3, then Rajdhani label caps. One variable per tier switches the font: <code>--r-font-heading</code> (h1, and h2 to h3 unless set apart), <code>--r-font-sub</code> (h2 to h3) and <code>--r-font-minor</code> (h4 to h6). Set one to <code>var(--r-font-text)</code> to turn Audiowide off there, or <code>--r-font-minor</code> to <code>var(--r-font-heading)</code> for more Audiowide.</p>
  <Notes
    markup={tiers}
    classes="None: `base.css` styles plain elements (headings, body, small, links, mark, kbd, code, quotes, lists, definitions, details, figures, `hr`, selection and the focus ring)."
    tokens="`--r-font-heading`, `--r-font-sub`, `--r-font-minor`, `--r-font-text`, `--r-font-mono`, `--r-font-brand`; colors `--r-text`, `--r-text-small`, `--r-text-dim`, `--r-heading` to `--r-heading-6`, `--r-link`, `--r-link-hover`, `--r-focus`."
    do="Write plain semantic HTML; the element rules sit in `:where()`, so any class of the app overrides them."
    dont="Pick a heading level for its look; retune the tier variables instead."
  />

  <h3 class="sc-subhead">Web and document</h3>
  <div class="sc-grid cols-2 sc-scales">
    <div>
      <p class="sc-cap"><b>Web</b> <code>base.css</code></p>
      <div>
        <h1>Mission control</h1>
        <h2>A quiet view from orbit</h2>
        <h3>Engineering log</h3>
        <p><DarkR /> is futuristic with a hint of retro, on a fresh palette you don't often see in everyday interfaces. It is made for night mode and for night-light filters that warm the screen in the evening. Its purples and magentas carry a lot of blue, so <DarkR /> changes more than most themes when the night light comes on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="sc-cap"><b>Document</b> <code>.r-doc</code> in <code>doc.css</code></p>
      <div class="r-doc">
        <h1>Mission control</h1>
        <h2>A quiet view from orbit</h2>
        <h3>Engineering log</h3>
        <p><DarkR /> is futuristic with a hint of retro, on a fresh palette you don't often see in everyday interfaces. It is made for night mode and for night-light filters that warm the screen in the evening. Its purples and magentas carry a lot of blue, so <DarkR /> changes more than most themes when the night light comes on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="sc-note">The web scale is the default. The document scale is for long text: Audiowide for h1 only, Rajdhani for h2 and h3, Saira for the body. Code is Monaspace Neon in both, <code>--r-font-mono</code>.</p>
  <Notes
    markup={doc}
    classes="`.r-doc` on the element that holds the document. Outside it the web scale applies."
    tokens="`--r-font-doc` (Saira), `--r-doc-measure` (68ch, the widest line)."
    do="Link `doc.css` only on pages that hold documents, after `base.css`."
    dont="Put interface controls inside `.r-doc`; it is a reading scale, not an app scale."
  />

  <h3 class="sc-subhead">Fonts</h3>
  <p class="sc-prose">The theme loads its fonts itself, from <code>../fonts/woff2/</code> next to <code>theme/</code>. Nothing else is needed in the page.</p>
  <Notes
    markup={fonts}
    do="Ship the licenses from `assets/fonts/licenses/` with the fonts."
    dont="Load the same faces from a web font service as well; the theme's own files are subset for the web."
  />

  <h3 class="sc-subhead">Prompt</h3>
  <p><span class="r-prompt">Click or press</span></p>
  <Notes
    markup={prompt}
    classes="`.r-prompt`: a call to act, in Bright green Audiowide caps."
    do="Use it for a short call to act next to the thing to act on."
    dont="Use it for a heading or a long sentence."
  />
</section>
